    <h2 class="sec-h">Built on a record of every business, and how they relate</h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">Every transaction is matched against it, including the long-tail, local, new, and third-party-routed charges other approaches miss.</p>

    <div class="graph-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="feat-list" id="feat-list">
          <div class="feat on" data-i="0"><div class="feat-h"><i>01</i>The long tail, down to the address</div><div class="feat-b"><div>Small, local, and new businesses other approaches miss, with the store's address.</div></div></div>
          <div class="feat" data-i="1"><div class="feat-h"><i>02</i>The business behind the third party</div><div class="feat-b"><div>The verified merchant behind a delivery app, a processor, an app store, or a marketplace, with the third party named alongside it.</div></div></div>
          <div class="feat" data-i="2"><div class="feat-h"><i>03</i>Every location, rolled up to its brand</div><div class="feat-b"><div>Every location connects to its brand, and every brand to its owner, so a reward or control set on a brand applies across its locations.</div></div></div>
          <div class="feat" data-i="3"><div class="feat-h"><i>04</i>Kept current as merchants change</div><div class="feat-b"><div>Merchant IDs (MIDs) rotate, processors change, businesses change hands, and a storefront can reopen on the same terminal as something else. Spade keeps pace, so the match holds.</div></div></div>
